# Curriculum Sections — Home & Nav Registry

The home page and header navigation are driven by **`data/curriculum_sections.yaml`**, not a hardcoded list. When adding a new top-level module under `content/<section>/`, register it there or it will not appear on `/`.

## Checklist for a New Section

1. **`data/curriculum_sections.yaml`** — append an entry:
   ```yaml
   - slug: my-new-section
     menuLabel: My New Section
   ```
   Order in this file controls home grid and nav order.

2. **`content/<section>/_index.md`** — section landing page (`title`, `description`, `draft: false`).

3. **Layouts** (match existing sections):
   - `layouts/<section>/list.html` and `single.html`
   - `layouts/partials/<section>-nav.html`
   - Add section name to `layouts/partials/extend_head.html` style guard if it uses `sd-section-nav` / TOC styles.

4. **Module data** (if module-grouped TOC): `data/<section>_modules.yaml` + `data/<section>_order.yaml`.

5. **Verify**: `hugo server` → `/` shows the new card; header nav includes the new link.

## What Updates Automatically

| Component | Source |
|-----------|--------|
| Home section grid | `curriculum_sections.yaml` + section `_index.md` description |
| Header nav links | `curriculum_sections.yaml` |
| Topic count on card | `len` of section `RegularPages` |

## Do Not

- Rely on the old paginated post feed on home — `layouts/index.html` is a curriculum hub only.
- Add curriculum sections only under `content/` without registering in `curriculum_sections.yaml`.

Reference sections: `system-fundamentals`, `system-design`, `database-internals`, `security-architecture`.
